  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Meet Me At The Creek** (1 review): The first Meet Me at the Creek included a Cosmic Highway tease and a Don't Lie tease [5]\n- **Shout Little Lulie / Liza Jane** (1 review): Encore had Billy playing banjo solo [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Dust In The Baggie**: rare: 9 archived performances [6]\n- **Come On Down The Mountain Katie Daly**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n- **Atlantic City**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n- **Riders On The Storm**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **Shout Little Lulie / Liza Jane**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2017-02-25.matrix** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 18 songs; 108 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Anders Beck and Paul Hoffman joined on Katie Daly's neighbouring stretch of the set, marked in the list through Meet Me at the Creek [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2017-02-25.matrix**: taped by Rob O'Brien; transferred by Rob O'Brien; source: Matrix - SBD + DPA 4021(DIN) > Sound Devices 744T(24/96) [1]. Also: Matrix of soundboard plus DPA 4021 mics, recorded to Sound Devices 744T at 24/96, then edited in Wave Lab and tracked; Mics were taped from front of board area, about eight feet high, third drink rail, thirty feet from stage [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings Bluebird Theater - Denver, CO - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/show/bluebird-theater-denver-co/) [7]",
